<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσσεβ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ungodly, impious,
			profane</i>, of persons, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				598
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			 or 
				Sup.
			), and their acts, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. χάρις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					514
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τῶν κακίστων δυσσεβέστατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OC</u>
					1190
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. μέλαθρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					694
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					825
				</span></i>
			.—This family of words is chiefly found in Trag.
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσσεβής</span> occurs in <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				540
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
				105
			</span></i>, and later Prose as <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				5.174b
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			)); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐσεβής</span>, etc., are
			freq. also in Prose.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
